# upstream/84-region-dce-iterative: region dead code elimination keeps its
# place on explicit stacks, so its native depth does not grow with the IR's
# nesting, and the greedy driver inside the upstream passes the pipeline
# runs on each lowered function keeps a small stack. Operations nested
# 10,000 deep, each level holding a dead cast, on a thread whose stack is
# 256 KiB: every dead cast is erased and every live operation stays where
# it was (dce.cpp). The nesting is built in memory: mlir-opt's parser
# recurses on the same depth through each operation's parse hook, so
# through mlir-opt region DCE is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "region DCE: 10,000 nested operations on a 256 KiB stack, each dead cast erased" "$here/dce.cpp" 10000
